prompt: Wide earthen rampart of Gia Định under a heavy overcast sky; work gangs with Vietnamese faces in brown tunics pound fresh earth into the wall with wooden rammers, others drive sharpened stakes along the moat and haul small bronze cannons up a ramp, the young lord stands small and off-center at about one-fifth frame height on a shaded wooden veranda of a watchtower looking out over the river, where dark storm clouds roll in and a few patrol boats circle. No Qing/Ming Chinese, 19th-century Nguyễn imperial or European elements.
